# Portfolio Site — Engineering Standards

This is a **static, dependency-free** site: `index.html` + `script.js` + `styles.css`. No build step, no framework. Keep it that way unless explicitly asked to add a toolchain.

## Core principles
- **No external JS dependencies.** Everything ships as plain `<script>` + native browser APIs. Do not introduce React, Tailwind, bundlers, or npm packages unless the user asks.
- **Self-contained & portable.** The site must open by double-clicking `index.html` (file://) or via any static server. No backend, no env vars required.
- **Accessibility first.** Use semantic HTML (`<nav>`, `<main>`, `<section>`, `<button>`). Every interactive control gets an `aria-label`. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Progressive enhancement.** JS enhances the page but the content must be readable with JS disabled.

## Code style
- HTML: lowercase tags/attrs, double quotes, 2-space indent, one element per line for clarity.
- CSS: kebab-case properties, single class selectors over deep nesting, group related rules with comment banners. Prefer CSS custom properties (`--color-bg`) for theming (the site already supports light/dark via `data-theme` or a class).
- JS: `const`/`let` over `var`, no `eval`, attach listeners with `addEventListener` (not inline `onclick`), wrap init in a DOMContentLoaded guard.
- Keep functions small and single-purpose. No code longer than ~40 lines per function without reason.

## Guardrails for the agent
- After editing, **re-read the file** and confirm there are no syntax errors (unclosed tags, unbalanced braces/parens, missing semicolons in JS).
- Do not leave dead code, commented-out blocks, or `console.log` debugging statements in committed output.
- Preserve the existing theme system (CSS variables + `#theme-toggle`). Any new color must be a variable, not a hardcoded hex.
- Keep bundle impact tiny — this is a personal site, not an app.

## Anti-patterns to avoid
- Don't add a framework or build tool because it's "modern."
- Don't inline large scripts in HTML — keep logic in `script.js`.
- Don't break the light/dark toggle when adding UI.
